local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:archmage-xylem"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Xylem",z="azshara",s="Archmage Xylem is an eccentric and reclusive human wizard dwelling in an isolated tower atop the cliffs of northern Azshara. Known for his volatile temperament and dangerous experiments, he has withdrawn from worldly affairs to pursue esoteric arcane research. Reaching him requires magical teleportation, and he only entertains adventurers who can assist in his peculiar studies or aid his personal vendettas.",h="Archmage Xylem is an eccentric and reclusive human wizard dwelling in an isolated tower atop the cliffs of...",sec={{t="A Recluse Above the Coast",b="Perched high upon the jagged cliffs of northern Azshara, Archmage Xylem makes his home in a secluded spire overlooking the ruined elven coastline. Rather than building a road or trail, the wizard isolated his sanctuary entirely, relying on his servant Sanath Lim-yo to magically transport approved visitors up the cliff face. Observers across Kalimdor consider him profoundly eccentric and perilous to deal with; even fellow scholars treat him with deep caution, noting that he behaves unlike almost any other human mage.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Third War",b="Before secluding himself in Azshara, Archmage Xylem took part in the Third War alongside the human expeditionary forces in Kalimdor. During the campaigns in the Stonetalon Mountains, his fortified encampment came under brutal assault by the Warsong clan, commanded by Grommash Hellscream. Though his defense was shattered in the fighting, Xylem survived the war, ultimately turning his back on large-scale military conflicts to pursue private arcane mastery in the wild reaches of the continent.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against Morphaz",b="Xylem's seclusion is not entirely peaceful; he harbors an intense grudge against the green dragonflight, specifically a drake named Morphaz. In the past, the beast devoured one of Xylem's unfortunate apprentices whole—swallowing an arcane shard of immense power along with the student. Rather than mourning the apprentice, the vengeful archmage remains fixated on hunting down Morphaz to extract the prized artifact from the dragon's belly.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How do you reach Archmage Xylem's tower?",a="Archmage Xylem's tower is set atop an inaccessible cliff in northern Azshara with no walkable path leading up. To reach him, you must locate his servant, Sanath Lim-yo, who stands near the base of the cliffs and can magically teleport travelers up to the tower grounds.",al={"get to xylem","reach xylem tower","teleport to xylem","xylem location"}},{q="Who is Archmage Xylem?",a="He is an eccentric human archmage who fought during the Third War in Stonetalon Mountains. Following the conflict, he withdrew to an isolated clifftop tower in northern Azshara to conduct dangerous arcane experiments away from civilization.",al={"who is xylem","archmage xylem lore","xylem background"}},{q="What happened to Xylem in the Third War?",a="During the Third War, Xylem commanded a human base in the Stonetalon Mountains. His outpost was assaulted and overrun by Grommash Hellscream and the blood-hazed Warsong clan, though the archmage survived the encounter.",al={"xylem third war","xylem stonetalon","xylem wc3"}},{q="Why does Xylem want the dragon Morphaz dead?",a="The green drake Morphaz attacked Xylem's followers and swallowed one of his apprentices whole. The apprentice was carrying a shard of vast arcane power, and Xylem seeks the drake's demise so the relic can be recovered from its stomach.",al={"xylem morphaz","why kill morphaz","morphaz shard"}},{q="Why do people say Xylem is dangerous?",a="Local contacts like Jediga warn travelers that Xylem is unpredictable, detached, and distinctly odd compared to other humans. He views apprentices primarily as material for his hazardous experiments and cares little for conventional safety or decorum.",al={"is xylem dangerous","xylem crazy","xylem personality"}},{q="Does Xylem belong to the Alliance or the Kirin Tor?",a="While originally part of the human expedition in the Third War, Xylem now operates as a thoroughly independent hermit. He does not actively serve the Alliance military and will readily deal with any adventurer willing to do his bidding, regardless of faction.",al={"xylem faction","is xylem alliance","xylem kirin tor"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, Xylem represents both supreme mastery and the unsettling consequence of total isolation in pursuit of magical power.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde veterans may recall clashing with Xylem's defenses in Stonetalon alongside Grommash Hellscream, yet the reclusive wizard is surprisingly willing to parley with Horde champions today.",["race:Human"]="Unlike the formal wizards of Dalaran or Stormwind, Xylem has entirely abandoned human society to live unbothered atop the wilds of Azshara."},kw={"arcane","archmage","azshara","morphaz","sanath lim-yo","stonetalon","tower","xylem"},rel={"zone:azshara","zone:stonetalon","topic:third-war","topic:warsong-clan","topic:grommash-hellscream"},src={"Archmage Xylem"}}
E["npc:azuregos"] = {t="npc",n="Azuregos",z="azshara",s="Azuregos is an eccentric blue dragon stationed along the coast of Azshara to protect ancient Highborne relics. Entrusted with safeguarding immense magical power by the Spell-Weaver Malygos, he prefers quiet study over violence, but he will readily swat aside any adventurer foolish enough to disturb his vigil.",h="Azuregos is an eccentric blue dragon stationed along the coast of Azshara to protect ancient Highborne relics.",sec={{t="The Guardian of Eldarath",b="Drawn to the magic-soaked shores of Azshara, Azuregos chose the ancient ruins of Eldarath as his sanctuary. Countless relics survived the Great Sundering along these shattered coasts, and Azuregos considers it his sacred duty as a servant of Malygos to keep such powerful artifacts away from careless mortals. Rather than lurking in a dark cave, he freely roams the crags and beaches, proudly dubbing himself the lord of all magic in the region. Though blessed with a sardonic sense of humor, he fiercely defends Azshara's treasures against the endless stream of adventurers seeking fame or plunder.",sp=0},{t="A Reluctant Custodian",b="Following the War of the Shifting Sands, Azuregos was saddled with safeguarding the Blue Scepter Shard—a fragmented key needed to break the barrier at the Scarab Wall. Despising the constant headaches, treasure-seekers, and would-be heroes drawn to the artifact, the clever drake eventually discarded the relic in the most unceremonious way imaginable: by feeding it to an empowered minnow named Maws, ensuring anyone hoping to claim the shard would have to dredge the depths rather than pester him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Azuregos?",a="Azuregos is a powerful blue dragon sent by the dragon aspect Malygos to patrol the ruins of Azshara. While many dragons are dour or wrathful, Azuregos is distinctly eccentric and witty, though he will mercilessly crush mortals who interrupt his magical studies or covet the treasures of Eldarath.",al={"azuregos lore","who is the blue dragon in azshara","azuregos background"}},{q="Why is Azuregos in Azshara?",a="He came to study and secure the potent arcane artifacts left behind by the ancient Highborne civilization after the Great Sundering. He guards the ruins of Eldarath against reckless plunderers seeking dangerous magic.",al={"why is azuregos here","what is azuregos doing in azshara","azuregos purpose"}},{q="What is his connection to the Scarab Wall?",a="After Archdruid Fandral Staghelm shattered the Scepter of the Shifting Sands, the shards were given to the four dragonflights for safekeeping. Azuregos was charged with protecting the Blue Scepter Shard, though he quickly grew tired of the attention it brought and hid it inside a magically altered minnow named Maws.",al={"azuregos scepter shard","azuregos shifting sands","shifting sands shard"},sp=1},{q="Why does his spirit appear in Azshara?",a="Azuregos is frequently attacked by raiding bands of adventurers seeking magical treasures or dragon scales. When slain, his spirit lingers near the shorelines, casually conversing with passerby while he awaits the rejuvenation of his physical form.",al={"spirit of azuregos","ghost azuregos","why is azuregos a ghost"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As an agent of the blue dragonflight, Azuregos embodies the mastery and regulation of the arcane, regarding mortal spellcasters as reckless children meddling with forces beyond their understanding.",["race:NightElf"]="Azuregos wanders among the shattered remnants of Eldarath, keeping vigilant watch over the very Highborne sorceries that nearly tore Kalimdor apart during the Sundering."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","bay of storms","blue dragon","eldarath","malygos","scepter shard","shifting sands"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:bay-of-storms","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:highborne","subzone:bear-s-head","subzone:bitter-reaches"},src={"Azuregos"}}
E["npc:duke-hydraxis"] = {t="npc",n="Duke Hydraxis",z="azshara",s="Duke Hydraxis is a noble water elemental commanding the Hydraxian Waterlords from a remote, wave-battered islet off the coast of Azshara. Pledged to Neptulon the Tidehunter, he rallies mortal adventurers to strike against his ancient elemental rivals, particularly Ragnaros the Firelord.",h="Duke Hydraxis is a noble water elemental commanding the Hydraxian Waterlords from a remote, wave-battered...",sec={{t="Lord of the Waterlords",b="Perched on a solitary rock northeast of the Ravencrest Monument in Azshara, Duke Hydraxis serves as the primary emissary of the Hydraxian Waterlords. While most elementals bound to Azeroth are hostile and chaotic, Hydraxis acts with measured purpose. As a devoted vassal of Neptulon the Tidehunter, he considers water the purest and most essential of the primal forces. He watches the rising turmoil across Azeroth with cold scrutiny, seeking champions capable of shifting the balance of elemental warfare.",sp=0},{t="The War Against Fire",b="Hydraxis's central campaign targets the blazing hosts of the Firelord, Ragnaros. He sees the encroachment of fiery elementals as a blight upon the world that must be extinguished. Before bestowing his trust or the tools needed to challenge Ragnaros's fiery stronghold in the Molten Core, Duke Hydraxis demands that mortals prove their strength, resilience, and loyalty by slaying hostile elementals across the continents. Those who prove their worth earn the blessings of the sea and the means to douse the sacred flames guarding the Firelord's domain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Duke Hydraxis be found?",a="Duke Hydraxis is situated on a tiny, isolated island off the eastern coast of Azshara, directly northeast of the Ravencrest Monument.",al={"where is hydraxis","duke hydraxis location","find duke hydraxis","hydraxis map spot"}},{q="Who is Duke Hydraxis aligned with?",a="He leads the Hydraxian Waterlords and serves Neptulon the Tidehunter, the elemental ruler of water.",al={"who does hydraxis serve","hydraxis faction","neptulon servant"}},{q="Why is Duke Hydraxis interested in mortal champions?",a="He seeks dependable mortal allies to wage war against the rival elemental factions, especially the fiery forces of Ragnaros lurking within Blackrock Mountain.",al={"why does hydraxis need us","what does hydraxis want","hydraxis purpose"}},{q="What is Duke Hydraxis's connection to the Molten Core?",a="Duke Hydraxis directs champions to undermine Ragnaros the Firelord and provides the elemental aids necessary to extinguish the runes and bosses guarding the Molten Core.",al={"hydraxis molten core","hydraxis ragnaros","mc hydraxis"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For shamans who commune directly with the primal elements, meeting an elemental of Duke Hydraxis's stature offers rare insight into the ancient hierarchy of Neptulon and the eternal rivalries between the elemental planes."},kw={"azshara","duke hydraxis","hydraxian waterlords","hydraxis","molten core","neptulon","ragnaros","water elemental"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ravencrest-monument","quest:99141"},src={"Duke Hydraxis"}}
E["npc:kalecgos"] = {t="npc",n="Kalecgos",z="azshara",s="Kalecgos, often calling himself Kalec, is a young blue dragon serving as an investigator for the Spell-Weaver Malygos. Preferring the guise of a humble half-elf, he is unusually sympathetic toward mortal races and deeply invested in safeguarding Azeroth's arcane balance.",h="Kalecgos, often calling himself Kalec, is a young blue dragon serving as an investigator for the Spell-Weaver...",sec={{t="A Dragon Among Mortals",b="Unlike many of his kin in the blue dragonflight who look upon mortals with detached indifference or outright suspicion, Kalecgos chooses to walk among them as an equal. Adopting the appearance of a half-elf with striking blue-black hair, he favors approachable mortal guises so he can navigate Azeroth directly. His empathetic nature sets him apart from older, more aloof drakes, though he remains fiercely devoted to his flight's sacred duty of stewarding magic.",sp=0},{t="The Quest for the Sunwell",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, Kalecgos was dispatched by Malygos to Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas to trace the lingering remnants of the shattered Sunwell. His mission plunged him into conflict with dwarven dragon hunters, Scourge agents, and the elven traitor Dar'Khan Drathir. Alongside his intended, Tyrygosa, and the human paladin Jorad Mace, Kalec uncovered the truth behind the avatar Anveena Teague, protecting the font of power from falling into undead clutches.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kalecgos?",a="Kalecgos is a young blue dragon who serves as an emissary and investigator for the blue dragonflight, sworn to safeguard arcane balance across Azeroth.",al={"who is kalec","what is kalecgos","kalecgos lore"}},{q="Why does Kalecgos appear as a half-elf?",a="Kalecgos chose the guise of a half-human, half-elf so he could walk among mortal races as an approachable friend and equal, rather than assuming a grandiose or intimidating form.",al={"kalec visage","why mortal form","kalec half elf"}},{q="What brought Kalecgos to Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas?",a="Malygos tasked him with investigating residual magical energies left behind after the Scourge destroyed the High Elves' font of power, the Sunwell.",al={"kalec sunwell","why was kalec in quelthalas"}},{q="What is his connection to Chronormu?",a="Kalecgos is a close friend of the bronze dragon Chronormu. Before Chromie chose her mortal gnome form, Kalec advised her on finding a visage that genuinely suited who she was.",al={"kalec chromie","chronormu visage kalec"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a member of the blue dragonflight, Kalecgos is inherently tied to the arcane, making his insights into magical currents and ley energy deeply fascinating to practitioners of the Kirin Tor."},kw={"anveena","blue dragon","kalec","kalecgos","malygos","sunwell","visage"},rel={"npc:chronormu","npc:lor-themar-theron","zone:hinterlands","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:third-war","topic:scourge","zone:azshara"},src={"Kalecgos"}}
E["npc:loramus-thalipedes"] = {t="npc",n="Loramus Thalipedes",z="azshara",s="Loramus Thalipedes is a reclusive night elf demon hunter secluded on a remote isle off the coast of Azshara. Flanked by loyal felhounds, he dedicates his existence to destroying Razelikh the Defiler, directing seasoned champions through rituals to strike down the dreadlord.",h="Loramus Thalipedes is a reclusive night elf demon hunter secluded on a remote isle off the coast of Azshara.",sec={{t="The Blind Hunter of the Isles",b="Perched on a solitary, storm-tossed island southeast of Hetaera's Clutch, Loramus Thalipedes stands apart from the rest of his kin. He is a demon hunter—an exile who underwent the agonizing ritual of blinding himself under his master's guidance to gain spectral sight. Surrounded by three towering felhounds named Raytaf, Shahiar, and Zaman, Loramus watches the unseen currents of demonic corruption across Azeroth while keeping a watchful vigil over the shattered ruins of Azshara.",sp=0},{t="A Vendetta Across Continents",b="Loramus's fixation lies across the sea in the Blasted Lands, focused entirely on the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler. Knowing that conventional steel cannot permanently end a cunning demon, Loramus guides travelers through ancient rituals, requiring them to gather enchanted Azsharite and reforge the legendary weapon Felbane. Through these esoteric preparations, he seeks to strip away Razelikh's wards, bind the demon's true name, and finish the vendetta once and for all.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Loramus Thalipedes?",a="Loramus Thalipedes is a night elf demon hunter residing on an isolated island off the coast of Azshara. He is dedicated to thwarting powerful demons, notably the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler.",al={"loramus identity","who is the demon hunter in azshara","who is loramus"}},{q="Why is Loramus blindfolded?",a="Like other demon hunters, Loramus removed his own eyes with the guidance of his master. In exchange for ordinary mortal vision, this ritual granted him the spectral sight necessary to detect demonic energies.",al={"why does loramus have no eyes","loramus blind","demon hunter blindfold"}},{q="Why are there felhounds guarding him?",a="Loramus has mastered and bound three powerful felhounds—Raytaf, Shahiar, and Zaman—turning their own predatory instincts toward serving his demonic hunts rather than the Burning Legion.",al={"loramus felhounds","why does loramus have demons","raytaf shahiar zaman"}},{q="What is his connection to the Blasted Lands?",a="He orchestrates the campaign to slay the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler, who rules the heights of the Blasted Lands. Loramus provides the crucial knowledge, rites, and weapons needed to pierce Razelikh's protections.",al={"loramus blasted lands","razelikh quest","why does he care about the blasted lands"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Night elves traditionally view demon hunters with profound horror and distrust, seeing their ritualistic self-mutilation and demonic pacts as an unforgivable path that mirrors the betrayal of the Illidari.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks will recognize his controlled felhounds as proof of exceptional demonic subjugation, though Loramus binds demons strictly to slaughter their own kind."},kw={"azshara","demon hunter","felbane","felhound","hetaera's clutch","loramus","razelikh","thalipedes"},rel={"zone:azshara","zone:blastedlands","subzone:hetaera-s-clutch","topic:night-elf","subzone:altar-of-storms-burning-steppes"},src={"Loramus Thalipedes"}}
E["npc:lord-arkkoroc"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Arkkoroc",z="azshara",s="Lord Arkkoroc is an ancient, towering sea giant who dwells within the ruined Temple of Arkkoran along the ragged coast of Azshara. Described by the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes as a lesser deity, he holds sway over the surrounding waters and commands lesser sea giants who serve as his sons.",h="Lord Arkkoroc is an ancient, towering sea giant who dwells within the ruined Temple of Arkkoran along the...",sec={{t="Lord of the Sunken Coast",b="Reclining amidst the brine-crusted ruins of the Temple of Arkkoran, Lord Arkkoroc is far more than a typical sea giant. To hermits like Loramus Thalipedes, this colossal being is considered a lesser deity whose divine will shapes the surrounding waters. His sons patrol the crags and shallows around the sanctuary, enforcing his quiet dominion over Azshara's tempestuous shores.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Against the Deep",b="Despite his immense divine power, Arkkoroc suffers personal losses beneath the tides. A fearsome, multi-headed hydra named Hetaera has hunted down and butchered many of his sons along the cliffs. Unable or unwilling to directly hunt the beast down, Arkkoroc barters valuable knowledge and occult aid to any wandering adventurer strong enough to present him with the heads of his offspring's killer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Arkkoroc?",a="Lord Arkkoroc is a massive sea giant who resides in the Temple of Arkkoran in Azshara. He is revered as a lesser deity of the seas and rules over a brood of sea giants whom he considers his sons.",al={"who is arkkoroc","arkkoroc lore","temple sea giant"}},{q="Where can I find Lord Arkkoroc?",a="You can find him perched amidst the ruins of the Temple of Arkkoran, located on the eastern coastline and rocky reefs of Azshara.",al={"arkkoroc location","where is arkkoroc","find arkkoroc"}},{q="Why does Loramus Thalipedes send adventurers to Arkkoroc?",a="Loramus Thalipedes directs travelers to Arkkoroc to seek arcane insights concerning a powerful demon. As a lesser sea deity, Arkkoroc holds ancient knowledge, but he demands that adventurers slay the hydra Hetaera before he parts with his secrets.",al={"loramus arkkoroc quest","name of the beast"}},{q="Why is Arkkoroc angry with the hydra Hetaera?",a="The savage sea beast Hetaera slaughtered several of Arkkoroc's sons who were patrolling the coastline. Seeking revenge for his slain kin, the sea giant demands her heads.",al={"why kill hetaera","arkkoroc hydra grudge"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins of the Temple of Arkkoran stand upon former Highborne lands, where an ancient sea entity now reigns supreme over the fallen majesty of old Kalimdor."},kw={"arkkoran","arkkoroc","azshara","hetaera","loramus","lord arkkoroc","sea giant"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","zone:azshara","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:naga"},src={"Lord Arkkoroc"}}
E["npc:magus-rimtori"] = {t="npc",n="Magus Rimtori",z="azshara",s="Magus Rimtori is a rogue blood elf sorceress leading an expedition among the ancient ruins of Azshara. Known for her ruthless deception, she manipulated the Horde into securing her passage across Kalimdor before butchering her orcish escort.",h="Magus Rimtori is a rogue blood elf sorceress leading an expedition among the ancient ruins of Azshara.",sec={{t="A Deadly Deception",b="Magus Rimtori led an expedition of high-borne blood elves across the sea to the ancient shores of Azshara. To ensure her party survived the perils of Kalimdor, she manipulated the orc Belgrom, charming and playing him until he agreed to supply an armed escort. Once the soldiers had delivered her safely to her destination, Rimtori revealed her true colors, turning on her protectors and massacring the entire garrison. Establishing her forces at the Thalassian Base Camp, she ventured out into the coastal wilds accompanied by elite bodyguards to hunt for forgotten magical artifacts.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Ruins",b="The true motive driving Rimtori's expedition remains clouded in secrecy, though her ruthless methods have earned her countless enemies. Aside from double-crossing the Horde, she also betrayed local hirelings, including the goblin surveyor Kim'jael, who claims she was obsessed with uncovering an ancient rune. Surrounded by relics such as a demonic summoning tome left behind in her camp, Rimtori's hunt for power has drawn the fierce retribution of the Horde she so callously crossed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Horde want Rimtori dead?",a="Rimtori charmed and manipulated the orc Belgrom into providing her expedition with a military escort across Kalimdor. Once they safely arrived in Azshara, she betrayed and slaughtered every single orcish soldier under Belgrom's command.",al={"why kill rimtori","belgrom rimtori lore","what did rimtori do to the horde"}},{q="Where can Magus Rimtori be found?",a="While her expedition established the Thalassian Base Camp, Rimtori herself roams the wilderness of Azshara accompanied by her personal blood elf bodyguards as she searches for ancient relics.",al={"rimtori location","where is magus rimtori","rimtori azshara location"}},{q="What was Rimtori searching for in Azshara?",a="According to the goblin Kim'jael, whom she hired and then betrayed, Rimtori was obsessively hunting for a mysterious ancient rune, alongside other potent relics such as a Kaldorei tome of summoning.",al={"what does rimtori want","rimtori purpose azshara","rimtori rune"}},{q="Who is Magister Hawkhelm?",a="Magister Hawkhelm is a blood elf officer entrusted by Magus Rimtori to command and supervise the Thalassian Base Camp while she investigates the surrounding ruins.",al={"hawkhelm","thalassian camp leader","magister hawkhelm rimtori"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Rimtori manipulated Belgrom and slaughtered the orc guard assigned to escort her, making her assassination a top priority for Horde warriors seeking to avenge their fallen kin.",["class:Mage"]="Rimtori demonstrates the lengths to which Thalassian magi will go in their desperate pursuit of arcane power, sifting through Kalimdor's ruins and demonic relics."},kw={"azshara","belgrom","blood elf","hawkhelm","kim'jael","magus rimtori","rimtori","thalassian base camp"},rel={"subzone:thalassian-base-camp","zone:azshara","topic:horde","topic:goblin"},src={"Magus Rimtori"}}
E["npc:ogtinc"] = {t="npc",n="Ogtinc",z="azshara",s="Ogtinc is an independent furbolg hunter perched on a high ridge overlooking the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara. Having parted ways with his tribe to serve the balance of nature, he acts as a trusted ally and mentor for the Cenarion Circle. Skilled hunters seeking to test their craft against the fiercest beasts of Kalimdor often seek out his guidance.",h="Ogtinc is an independent furbolg hunter perched on a high ridge overlooking the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara.",sec={{t="A Furbolg Apart",b="While most furbolg in Kalimdor remain fiercely bound to their tribes—or have succumbed to corruption following the Third War—Ogtinc chose a distinct path. Departing from his kin, he dedicated his bow and survival lore to aiding the Cenarion Circle. He makes his camp high on a bluff southeast of Timbermaw Hold, vigilantly watching over the ancient, shattered lands of Azshara.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Hunt",b="Ogtinc is renowned among seasoned trackers for his intimate understanding of Kalimdor's wilderness. He tests hunters who have honed their skills across the continents, dispatching them to gather rare trophies—such as the antlers of courser beasts, the scale of wave-thrashed sea serpents, and parts from green dragonkin. Through these trials, he teaches that true hunting honors the natural world and preserves balance rather than mindlessly taking life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ogtinc?",a="Ogtinc is an accomplished furbolg hunter stationed atop the cliffs of Azshara. Unlike most of his reclusive or corrupted brethren, he left his ancestral tribe behind to offer his tracking skills and wisdom to the druids of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is ogtinc","ogtinc lore","furbolg in azshara"}},{q="Where can Ogtinc be found?",a="He is located in Azshara, perched on a cliffside campsite that overlooks the ancient Ruins of Eldarath, just southeast of Timbermaw Hold.",al={"where is ogtinc","ogtinc location","how to find ogtinc"}},{q="Why did Ogtinc leave his tribe?",a="Ogtinc left his kin specifically to aid the Cenarion Circle in their efforts to preserve nature. While his precise tribal origins remain unspecified, his clear mind and peaceable demeanor stand in stark contrast to the corrupted tribes elsewhere in northern Kalimdor.",al={"why did ogtinc leave","ogtinc tribe","is ogtinc timbermaw"}},{q="What role does Ogtinc play for hunters?",a="Ogtinc serves as a master mentor for veteran hunters reaching the pinnacle of their training. He tasks them with tracking down fearsome beasts across Kalimdor—from swift coursers to the brood of the Green Dragonflight—to prove their mastery of the wild.",al={"ogtinc hunter quests","hunter trainer ogtinc","why visit ogtinc"}},{q="Is Ogtinc affiliated with Timbermaw Hold?",a="While he camps near Timbermaw Hold, Ogtinc acts independently in direct partnership with the Cenarion Circle. He is naturally friendly toward travelers who approach peacefully, regardless of their standing with the Timbermaw tribe.",al={"ogtinc timbermaw","timbermaw reputation ogtinc","is ogtinc friendly"}},{q="Why does Ogtinc watch over the Ruins of Eldarath?",a="His vantage point high above the ruins gives him an unobstructed view of the troubled wilderness below, where naga, elementals, and lingering magical echoes threaten the delicate balance of the coastal forest.",al={"why is ogtinc in azshara","eldarath ogtinc","ogtinc cliff"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Ogtinc offers deep spiritual and practical trials for seasoned hunters, testing their marksmanship and survival skills against Kalimdor's deadliest creatures.",["class:Druid"]="As a steadfast partner of the Cenarion Circle, Ogtinc represents a rare bridge between the wild wisdom of uncorrupted furbolgs and the stewardship of the druids."},kw={"azshara","cenarion","eldarath","furbolg","hunter","ogtinc","timbermaw"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:furbolg","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:timbermaw-hold"},src={"Ogtinc"}}
E["subzone:bay-of-storms"] = {t="subzone",n="Bay of Storms",z="azshara",s="The Bay of Storms is an expansive, tempestuous gulf carving into the rugged eastern cliffs of Azshara. Its churning waters harbor ancient ruins, submerged caverns, and perilous marine beasts that make seafaring along this coast hazardous.",h="The Bay of Storms is an expansive, tempestuous gulf carving into the rugged eastern cliffs of Azshara.",sec={{t="A Tempestuous Coast",b="Opening out toward the Great Sea, the Bay of Storms defines much of Azshara's dramatic coastal geography. Far from a tranquil harbor, its turbulent waters and rocky outcrops are home to dangerous wildlife and ancient aquatic threats. Within and along its waters lie landmarks like the sunken Temple of Arkkoran, the coral reefs of Hetaera's Clutch, and Scalebeard's Cave, leaving the bay largely avoided by casual sailors and claimed instead by coastal monsters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Bay of Storms located?",a="The Bay of Storms sits on the eastern edge of Azshara, opening directly into the Great Sea off the coast of Kalimdor.",al={"bay of storms location","where is bay of storms","where is the bay"}},{q="What notable landmarks lie within the bay?",a="The bay contains several notable coastal features, including the Temple of Arkkoran, the reef known as Hetaera's Clutch, and the hidden retreat of Scalebeard's Cave.",al={"landmarks in bay of storms","what is in bay of storms","bay of storms points of interest"}},{q="Why is the bay dangerous to navigate?",a="Violent surf, sharp jagged rocks, and hostile aquatic creatures make the bay treacherous for passing ships, and little coastal civilization exists here to offer rescue.",al={"is bay of storms safe","why dangerous","bay hazards"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The turbulent, deep sea waters of the Bay of Storms are famed among coastal fishermen seeking rare and prized deep-water catches off Kalimdor's coast."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","great sea","hetaera's clutch","scalebeard's cave","temple of arkkoran"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:hetaera-s-clutch"},src={"Bay of Storms"}}
E["subzone:bear-s-head"] = {t="subzone",n="Bear's Head",z="azshara",s="Bear's Head is a secluded mountainous stretch along the southeastern cliffs of Azshara. Named for the resident Timbermaw furbolgs whose settlements dot the rugged high ground, it serves as an outpost linked to their larger homes farther north while lying directly beneath the cliffside sanctum of Archmage Xylem.",h="Bear's Head is a secluded mountainous stretch along the southeastern cliffs of Azshara.",sec={{t="Furbolg Outposts and Cliffside Magic",b="Tucked away in southeastern Azshara, Bear's Head takes its name from the encampments of uncorrupted Timbermaw furbolgs established upon its heights. These rustic settlements act as outlying camps tied to the major furbolg dens of Ursolan and Timbermaw Hold to the north. Perched atop the looming cliffs directly above the area sits Xylem's Tower, an eccentric sanctuary where Archmage Xylem and his small retinue of apprentices conduct arcane studies in quiet isolation from the rest of the troubled coastline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called Bear's Head?",a="The region is named after the Timbermaw furbolg villages established throughout its hills. The bear-folk maintain active encampments here, which serve as southern outposts for their strongholds in northern Kalimdor.",al={"bear's head name origin","why bears head","bears head meaning"}},{q="Which furbolgs live in Bear's Head?",a="The area is populated by the Timbermaw tribe. Unlike many other furbolg tribes across Kalimdor who fell victim to demonic corruption, the Timbermaw have largely resisted the taint and remain connected to their principal settlements at Ursolan and Timbermaw Hold.",al={"bears head furbolgs","timbermaw in bears head","what furbolg tribe is here"}},{q="What is the tower on the cliffs above Bear's Head?",a="The cliffside spire belongs to Archmage Xylem. He is an eccentric human wizard who retreated from Dalaran to Azshara to pursue his studies in seclusion, accompanied by a handful of apprentices and high elven associates.",al={"tower above bears head","who lives in the tower here","xylem tower"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The towering cliff overlooking Bear's Head is home to Archmage Xylem, a powerful and eccentric spellcaster sought out by practitioners of the arcane seeking advanced training."},kw={"archmage xylem","azshara","bear's head","bears head","furbolg","timbermaw","ursolan"},rel={"zone:azshara","npc:archmage-xylem","topic:furbolg","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:ursolan"},src={"Bear's Head"}}
E["subzone:bitter-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Bitter Reaches",z="azshara",s="The Bitter Reaches is a rugged, windswept wilderness in northeastern Azshara. Largely untouched by civilization, the rugged cliffs are prowled by predatory beasts and massive mountain giants.",h="The Bitter Reaches is a rugged, windswept wilderness in northeastern Azshara.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Coastal Frontier",b="Occupying the northeastern cliffs of Azshara, the Bitter Reaches remains a stark and untamed stretch of rocky terrain overlooking the Great Sea. Flocks of feral hippogryphs and two-headed chimaeras nest amidst the heights, while acidic oozes seep through the cold ground. Along the high northern ridges, colossal mountain giants have claimed the slopes as their own, driving away lesser creatures and turning the frozen approaches into a perilous hazard for any solitary traveler.",sp=0},{t="Flora of the Crags",b="Despite the harsh winds and aggressive predators, the craggy landscape sustains rare mountain flora. Sparse clusters of Mountain Silversage cling to the high rock faces and windy perches, making the dangerous terrain occasionally worth traversing for intrepid herbalists daring enough to avoid the giants and territorial chimaeras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Bitter Reaches?",a="The Bitter Reaches form the northeastern quadrant of Azshara, covering the high coastal cliffs and ridges above the bay.",al={"bitter reaches location","where is bitter reaches","bitter reaches azshara"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The region is home to territorial hippogryphs, two-headed chimaeras, and oozes. Towering mountain giants roam the northern boundary.",al={"bitter reaches mobs","what lives in bitter reaches","monsters in bitter reaches"}},{q="Why are there mountain giants here?",a="The ancient mountain giants inhabit the high northern peaks and edges of Azshara, carving out their own territory and driving out most local wildlife from their stomping grounds.",al={"mountain giants azshara","why are giants in bitter reaches"}},{q="What valuable resources grow in the Bitter Reaches?",a="Rare high-altitude herbs such as Mountain Silversage can be found growing sparsely across the rocky outcrops and ridgelines.",al={"herbs bitter reaches","bitter reaches gathering"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The wind-battered heights of the Bitter Reaches are one of the few places in Azshara where prized Mountain Silversage grows, though you will have to contend with chimaeras and giants to harvest it.",["class:Hunter"]="The cliffside aeries of the Bitter Reaches are prime hunting territory, teeming with wild hippogryphs and aggressive chimaeras native to the ancient coastline."},kw={"azshara","bitter reaches","chimaera","hippogryph","mountain giant","mountain silversage","ooze"},rel={"zone:azshara"},src={"Bitter Reaches"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Ridge",z="azshara",s="Forlorn Ridge is a towering mountain ridge looming over southwestern Azshara. Its strategic elevation and commanding views over the coast have drawn the attention of both the Alliance and the Horde, who have each carved out fortifications along its slopes.",h="Forlorn Ridge is a towering mountain ridge looming over southwestern Azshara.",sec={{t="A Contested Vantage",b="Rising sharply above the autumnal forests of western Azshara, Forlorn Ridge dominates the surrounding terrain. Resembling an ancient, long-dormant volcano, its high vantage point offers a sweeping view over the coastal approaches and the ruined elven estates below. Because control over these heights dictates military dominance in the sector, both Alliance and Horde forces have established encampments and outposts along its mountain flanks, watching each other warily across the rugged bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Forlorn Ridge?",a="Forlorn Ridge is a prominent mountain feature situated in southwestern Azshara, towering over the local wilderness and coastal roads.",al={"where is forlorn ridge","forlorn ridge azshara","what is this mountain"}},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting over this ridge?",a="The ridge commands unmatched sightlines across western Azshara. Whoever holds the high ground can monitor troop movements between the coastal ruins and the inland passes, prompting both factions to fortify positions on its slopes.",al={"why are there camps here","who controls forlorn ridge","alliance vs horde forlorn ridge"}},{q="Was Forlorn Ridge originally a volcano?",a="The distinct shape and rugged composition of the mountain suggest it may have been a volcanic formation in the distant past, though it has long since grown quiet and overgrown.",al={"is forlorn ridge a volcano","volcano in azshara"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Holding the heights of Forlorn Ridge provides early warning and tactical oversight against Horde movements spilling eastward out of the Barrens and Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, establishing footholds along Forlorn Ridge helps secure the rugged borderlands of Azshara just north of Durotar against Alliance incursions."},kw={"azshara","forlorn ridge","fortifications","mountain","ruins of eldarath","volcano"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:horde","topic:alliance","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath"},src={"Forlorn Ridge"}}
E["subzone:haldarr-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Haldarr Encampment",z="azshara",s="The Haldarr Encampment is a corrupted satyr outpost nestled in western Azshara, situated northeast of the Shadowsong Shrine and southwest of Valormok. Densely inhabited by the vicious Haldarr satyrs, it stands as a dangerous blight among the ancient elven ruins. It is also the site where an injured Night Elf Sentinel, Keldara Sunblade, is held captive.",h="The Haldarr Encampment is a corrupted satyr outpost nestled in western Azshara, situated northeast of the...",sec={{t="A Den of Demon-Spawn",b="Perched among the broken stones of western Azshara, the Haldarr Encampment serves as a gathering ground for the Haldarr clan of satyrs. These twisted creatures, ancient remnants of the Highborne cursed by demonic corruption during the Sundering, actively hunt and harass any who traverse the autumn forests. The dense settlement poses an ongoing threat to both the Horde forces stationed at nearby Valormok and the dwindling Night Elf sentinels trying to monitor the region.",sp=0},{t="The Captured Sentinel",b="Amid the encampment's fiendish inhabitants lies Sentinel Keldara Sunblade, stranded and injured in the heart of enemy territory. Her presence within the camp makes the Haldarr Encampment an urgent concern for those seeking to disrupt the satyrs' foul activities and unravel why she remains pinned down among demonic captors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Haldarr Encampment?",a="The Haldarr Encampment is a corrupted settlement in western Azshara controlled by the Haldarr clan of satyrs. It lies southwest of the Horde outpost of Valormok and northeast of Shadowsong Shrine.",al={"haldarr encampment lore","what is haldarr","who lives in haldarr encampment"}},{q="Who are the Haldarr?",a="The Haldarr are a vicious sect of satyrs inhabiting Azshara. Like all satyrs, they descend from ancient Night Elves who embraced demonic pacts during the War of the Ancients, cursed into goat-legged fiends serving the remnants of the Burning Legion's will.",al={"haldarr satyrs","who are the satyrs here"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Keldara Sunblade?",a="Sentinel Keldara Sunblade is a wounded Night Elf found held inside the Haldarr Encampment, surrounded by hostile satyrs who keep her trapped within their territory.",al={"keldara sunblade","injured night elf","who is the captive here"}},{q="Why is this camp dangerous to nearby travelers?",a="The camp is densely populated by aggressive satyrs who actively patrol and threaten the surrounding paths, endangering both Horde operations out of Valormok and any wandering scouts in the area.",al={"is haldarr dangerous","why clear haldarr"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the Haldarr satyrs are a shameful, enduring reminder of the ancient Highborne's descent into demonic madness, and saving Sentinel Keldara Sunblade from their clutches is a matter of duty.",["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just southwest of Valormok, this dense nest of demons poses an immediate threat to Horde scouts and supply lines pushing across Azshara's cliffs."},kw={"azshara","encampment","haldarr","keldara sunblade","satyr","shadowsong shrine","valormok"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:satyr","subzone:valormok","subzone:shadowsong-shrine"},src={"Haldarr Encampment"}}
E["subzone:hetaera-s-clutch"] = {t="subzone",n="Hetaera's Clutch",z="azshara",s="Hetaera's Clutch is a sunken night elven temple dedicated to Elune, nestled deep beneath the churning waters of Azshara's Bay of Storms. Once a sacred site of devotion, the submerged ruins are now overrun by deadly hydras hatched by their broodmother, Hetaera. Adventurers braving the depths will find ancient stonework claimed by vicious aquatic predators.",h="Hetaera's Clutch is a sunken night elven temple dedicated to Elune, nestled deep beneath the churning waters...",sec={{t="A Drowned Sanctuary",b="Before the Great Sundering tore ancient Kalimdor apart, this structure served as a grand temple dedicated to the moon goddess Elune. Cast into the depths of the Bay of Storms, its stone pillars and sacred halls have spent ten thousand years beneath the sea. Today, all signs of holy veneration have been swallowed by the tides, leaving behind a solemn monument to the lost Kaldorei empire.",sp=0},{t="Domain of the Broodmother",b="The submerged sanctuary has taken on a far deadlier identity as the nesting ground of Hetaera, a massive multi-headed hydra who stalks the nearby coastal waters and rocky isles. Her numerous offspring, the Spawn of Hetaera, prowl through the ruined arches and corridors of the drowned temple, attacking any surface-dweller bold enough to dive into the bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Hetaera's Clutch originally built for?",a="Long before it sank beneath the waves, this structure was a magnificent temple dedicated to the moon goddess, Elune. It was built during the peak of the ancient night elven empire before being cast into the ocean during the Great Sundering.",al={"what is hetaeras clutch","what was this temple","hetaera clutch lore"}},{q="Where is Hetaera's Clutch located?",a="The Clutch rests deep underwater within the Bay of Storms, located off the jagged southern coast of Azshara.",al={"where is hetaeras clutch","hetaera clutch location","how to find hetaera clutch"}},{q="Who is Hetaera?",a="Hetaera is a ferocious three-headed hydra who prowls the waters of Azshara. While her children infest the sunken temple itself, Hetaera is typically found swimming slightly to the north of the Clutch or basking on nearby offshore islands.",al={"who is hetaera","where is hetaera","what is hetaera"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the submerged ruins?",a="The drowned halls are swarming with Hetaera's brood, vicious aquatic hydras known to defend their nesting site against any intruders who swim too close.",al={"what mobs are in hetaeras clutch","what lives in hetaera clutch"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing a sacred sanctuary of Elune submerged and desecrated as a nest for feral hydras is a painful reminder of the civilization torn away during the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Aquatic druids exploring the depths of the Bay of Storms must remain cautious, as the hydras claiming this ancient sanctuary are extremely hostile to trespassers."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","elune","hetaera","hetaera's clutch","hetaeras clutch","hydra","sunken temple","temple of elune"},rel={"subzone:bay-of-storms","zone:azshara","topic:elune"},src={"Hetaera's Clutch"}}
E["subzone:horizon-scout"] = {t="subzone",n="Horizon Scout",z="azshara",s="The Horizon Scout is a sunken vessel resting on the ocean floor in the Ruined Reaches off the southern coast of Azshara. While its captain remains stranded ashore, several crew members remain trapped in the submerged hull, kept alive beneath the waves by an arcane water-breathing enchantment.",h="The Horizon Scout is a sunken vessel resting on the ocean floor in the Ruined Reaches off the southern coast...",sec={{t="Trapped on the Ocean Floor",b="Resting beneath the waves among the treacherous shoals of the Ruined Reaches, the Horizon Scout met a violent end off Azshara's jagged coast. While Captain Vanessa Beltis managed to reach land on a nearby peninsula, a portion of the crew went down with the hull. Miraculously, the survivors inside have not drowned; a gnome named Roland Geardabbler maintains a sustained magical bubble of water breathing that preserves them within the wreckage. Surrounded by hostile aquatic predators and predatory naga, the remaining sailors wait in the dark forward compartments, unable to surface on their own.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Ambush",b="Evidence aboard the ship hints at the sinister forces behind its destruction. In the forward stairwell lies a small shard of raw Azsharite, a mysterious mineral unique to these shores. The Spitelash naga prowling the waters around the Ruined Reaches likely struck the Horizon Scout to plunder whatever artifacts or resources the expedition carried, dragging the vessel down to ensure no survivors could escape with secrets or treasures of the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Horizon Scout located?",a="The wreck of the Horizon Scout sits submerged at the bottom of the bay in the Ruined Reaches, located off the southern coast of Azshara.",al={"horizon scout location","where is horizon scout","find horizon scout"}},{q="How is the crew still alive underwater?",a="A gnomish engineer or mage named Roland Geardabbler continuously channels an aura of water breathing inside the sunken hull, keeping the trapped crew members alive in a sustained pocket of breathable air.",al={"how are they breathing","why crew not dead","roland geardabbler aura"}},{q="Who is Captain Vanessa Beltis?",a="Captain Vanessa Beltis is the commander of the Horizon Scout. Unlike the sailors trapped in the hull, she managed to reach the safety of Azshara's southern peninsula alongside a few stranded survivors.",al={"vanessa beltis","horizon scout captain","ship captain"}},{q="What caused the Horizon Scout to sink?",a="The ship was almost certainly ambushed and sunk by the local Spitelash naga. A piece of raw Azsharite resting in the lower deck suggests the naga attacked to seize whatever mineral riches or artifacts the expedition had gathered.",al={"why did horizon scout sink","who sank horizon scout","what happened to the ship"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The entire surviving crew owes their breath to Roland Geardabbler, whose relentless spellcasting holds back the ocean depths inside the flooded hull.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Horizon Scout represents a disastrous Alliance-aligned maritime venture into the perilous waters of Azshara, leaving its crew divided between the shore and a watery tomb."},kw={"azshara shipwreck","azsharite","horizon scout","roland geardabbler","ruined reaches","spitelash","vanessa beltis"},rel={"subzone:ruined-reaches","zone:azshara","topic:naga","subzone:faldir-s-cove"},src={"Horizon Scout"}}
E["subzone:jagged-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Jagged Reef",z="azshara",s="The Jagged Reef forms the rugged northern coast of Azshara, where sandy beaches meet jagged stone spurs and churning surf. Treacherous rocks lurk beneath the shallow water, making maritime travel impossible. The desolate shore is primarily populated by prowling hydras, scavenging makrura, and territorial murloc tribes.",h="The Jagged Reef forms the rugged northern coast of Azshara, where sandy beaches meet jagged stone spurs and...",sec={{t="A Perilous Shoreline",b="Stretching across Azshara's northern edge, the Jagged Reef is a harsh littoral expanse where broken cliffs and jutting stone outcroppings divide the sandy shores into secluded inlets. Beneath the breaking waves lie submerged crags and shifting shallows, turning the waters into a graveyard for any vessel foolish enough to venture near. On land, the wild coastline offers little comfort; salt-crusted beasts, predatory hydras, and aggressive makrura wander the surf line alongside entrenched murlocs scouring the tides for scraps and unwary prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jagged Reef located?",a="The Jagged Reef encompasses the northern coastline of Azshara, spanning stretches of beach, rocky jets, and small ocean inlets along the region's northern shores.",al={"jagged reef location","where is jagged reef"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Jagged Reef?",a="The coast is teeming with dangerous aquatic life, including aggressive murlocs, ravenous multi-headed hydras, and armored makrura scouring both the shallow waters and the sandy beach.",al={"what lives here","jagged reef mobs","monsters in jagged reef"}},{q="Can ships navigate the waters around the Jagged Reef?",a="No. The area earns its name from the sheer abundance of treacherous underwater rocks and erratic shallows, making maritime navigation through the reef virtually suicidal for any ship.",al={"can boats sail here","jagged reef shipping"}},{q="Are there any settlements along the reef?",a="There are no civilized settlements along the Jagged Reef. Aside from transient explorers or hunters, the only organized presence comes from wild murloc encampments scattered across the shore.",al={"towns near jagged reef","who lives at jagged reef"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The exposed northern beaches offer abundant opportunities to study or tame native amphibious beasts such as hydras and shoreline crustaceans."},kw={"azshara","beach","coast","hydras","jagged reef","makrura","murlocs","shallows"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:murloc"},src={"Jagged Reef"}}
E["subzone:lake-mennar"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Mennar",z="azshara",s="Lake Mennar is a tranquil body of freshwater nestled amidst the shattered ruins of Azshara. It is remarkably renowned as one of the exceedingly rare havens outside of Northrend where members of the blue dragonflight reside. While the perimeter teems with protective blue dragonspawn, the shores of the lake itself remain strangely serene.",h="Lake Mennar is a tranquil body of freshwater nestled amidst the shattered ruins of Azshara.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary for the Blue Dragonflight",b="Situated in the ancient, broken landscape of Azshara, Lake Mennar serves as a secluded gathering ground for the blue dragonflight. Aside from Mazthoril to the north in Winterspring, it is virtually unheard of to encounter blue dragons in such numbers across Kalimdor. Blue dragonspawn tirelessly patrol the ridges and approaches circling the basin, fiercely guarding the waters. Yet for any wanderer daring enough to slip through this vigilant ring of sentries, the calm waters of the lake offer unexpected quietude, shielded from the arcane turmoil and roaming beast packs common to the rest of the peninsula.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there blue dragons at Lake Mennar?",a="Lake Mennar holds a quiet, special significance to the blue dragonflight, making it one of their very few gathering grounds on Kalimdor outside of Mazthoril in Winterspring. Dragonspawn vigilantly patrol the perimeter to safeguard the basin and keep interlopers away from their brood.",al={"why blue dragons here","who lives at lake mennar","blue dragonflight lake mennar"}},{q="Is Lake Mennar dangerous to visit?",a="The surrounding ridges and approaches are heavily patrolled by aggressive blue dragonkin and whelps. However, the water and immediate shoreline inside the basin are surprisingly peaceful if you manage to slip past the outer ring of guards.",al={"is lake mennar safe","enemies at lake mennar"}},{q="How does Lake Mennar connect to other blue dragon roosts?",a="On the continent of Kalimdor, Lake Mennar and Mazthoril in Winterspring are the primary known territories watched over by the blue flight. Both sites serve as rare outposts far to the south of the flight's ancestral home in Northrend.",al={"connection to mazthoril","lake mennar winterspring"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As stewards of the world's arcane energies, the blue dragons guarding Lake Mennar make the basin an area of great intrigue and caution for practitioners of arcane magic."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","blue dragonflight","dragonspawn","lake mennar","mazthoril","whelps"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:mazthoril","npc:azuregos","zone:winterspring"},src={"Lake Mennar"}}
E["subzone:ravencrest-monument"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravencrest Monument",z="azshara",s="Perched upon the windswept cliffs of southern Azshara, the Ravencrest Monument marks the shattered remnant of an ancient night elven colossus. Once a towering tribute overlooking the Great Sea, the statue has long since broken apart, leaving only towering legs and scattered stone ruins now stalked by hostile Spitelash naga.",h="Perched upon the windswept cliffs of southern Azshara, the Ravencrest Monument marks the shattered remnant of...",sec={{t="Ruins of a Colossus",b="Standing high above the ocean southeast of the Ruins of Eldarath, the Ravencrest Monument was once an awe-inspiring marvel of Kaldorei stonework. Today, little remains of the majestic colossus beyond its pair of gigantic broken legs rooted to the stone plinth, with the shattered fragments of its torso and head either buried in the cliffside dirt or lost beneath the waves below. Reaching this remote coastal promontory requires trekking across the mainland bridges of Azshara, as sheer, rocky drops prevent any approach from the sea.",sp=0},{t="A Forgotten Legacy",b="Scholars often speculate that the monument commemorates Lord Kur'talos Ravencrest, the famed noble who rallied and led the night elven host during the War of the Ancients after the fall of Zin-Azshari. However, its close proximity to the pre-Sundering city of Eldarath and ambiguous surviving stonework leave its true origins debated. Rather than pilgrims or night elven caretakers, the surrounding cliff is currently claimed by the serpentine Spitelash naga, who defend the fallen monument with vicious territorial aggression.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ravencrest Monument?",a="It is the ruined base of a massive night elven colossus located on a coastal promontory in southern Azshara. Only its gigantic stone legs still stand upright, while the rest of the sculpture lies shattered and scattered across the clifftop.",al={"ravencrest statue","what is this statue","giant legs azshara"}},{q="Who was the monument built to honor?",a="It bears the name of House Ravencrest, most famous for Lord Kur'talos Ravencrest, the noble commander who led the mortal resistance against the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. However, because it sits near the ancient ruins of Eldarath, it is unclear whether it honors Kur'talos directly or an earlier ancestor from before the Great Sundering.",al={"who is ravencrest","who is the statue of","kurtalos ravencrest"}},{q="How do you reach the monument?",a="The monument cannot be climbed or entered from the sea due to sheer cliffs. Travelers must navigate through southern Azshara by land, crossing over stone bridges near the Ruins of Eldarath to reach the promontory.",al={"how to get to ravencrest monument","ravencrest path","ravencrest access"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the monument today?",a="The clifftop and surrounding terraces are infested with the Spitelash naga, making any exploration of the ancient ruins perilous for solitary travelers.",al={"what lives here","monument enemies","azshara naga"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the monument is a sobering reminder of the ancient Kaldorei Empire and the noble lineage of Ravencrest, whose heroic resistance in the War of the Ancients saved Azeroth from demonic annihilation.",["class:Warrior"]="The Ravencrest name carries mythic weight among battle commanders, as Kur'talos Ravencrest was the foremost general of the mortal forces during the catastrophic invasion of the Burning Legion."},kw={"azshara","colossus","eldarath","kurtalos ravencrest","ravencrest","ravencrest monument","spitelash","statue"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","topic:night-elf","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:naga","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Ravencrest Monument"}}
E["subzone:ruined-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruined Reaches",z="azshara",s="The Ruined Reaches comprise the treacherous southern coastline of Azshara near the border with Durotar. Marked by crumbling ancient ruins, shattered shipwrecks, and jagged shallows, these beaches are overrun by aggressive shoreline predators. Amid the desolation, a small gnomish outpost perches high on a cliffside above the surf.",h="The Ruined Reaches comprise the treacherous southern coastline of Azshara near the border with Durotar.",sec={{t="A Battered Coast",b="Stretching along the southern borders of Azshara just north of Durotar, the Ruined Reaches are a maze of rocky inlets, cliff faces, and debris-strewn sand. Like the Jagged Reef further north, hidden shallows make maritime travel extremely hazardous, leaving numerous ruined vessels broken along the shore. The waters and beaches teem with hostile wildlife, including territorial murlocs, vicious hydras, and armored makrura, making overland transit just as dangerous as navigating the surf.",sp=0},{t="The Gadgetspring Outpost",b="Perched upon a western cliff overlooking the beaches sits an unexpected pocket of tinker civilization: a gnomish workshop accessible via a steep trail from Azshara's mainland. Run by Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring, this outpost offers engineering components and general trade goods to passing adventurers. The interior features an elevator ascending to private quarters with three beds, though who—if anyone—claims the third bunk remains a quiet domestic mystery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Ruined Reaches located?",a="They form the southernmost coastal strip of Azshara, bordering the northern edge of Durotar. The area consists of sandy beaches, coastal inlets, and cliffs beneath the mainland bluffs.",al={"ruined reaches location","where is ruined reaches","how to get to ruined reaches"}},{q="What threats inhabit this stretch of coast?",a="The beaches and shallow waters are populated by hostile wildlife, primarily aggressive tribes of murlocs, multi-headed hydras, and makrura lurking along the tidal flats.",al={"ruined reaches mobs","what lives here","monsters in ruined reaches"}},{q="Who lives in the gnomish structure on the cliffs?",a="Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring live and work there. They run a small shop offering engineering parts and trade supplies to travelers navigating the desolate coast.",al={"gnomes in ruined reaches","gadgetspring house","who lives in the gnome house"}},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks here?",a="Like the neighboring Jagged Reef, the coastal waters are riddled with shallow rocks and hidden hazards that routinely catch ships unaware, dashing them against the cliffs.",al={"shipwrecks in azshara","why are ships wrecked here","ruined reaches wrecks"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The lonely workshop run by Blimo and Jubie Gadgetspring provides valuable parts and supplies for engineers exploring the wilds of Azshara.",["race:Gnome"]="Finding a high-tech gnomish homestead thriving on the hostile cliffs of Azshara is a welcome reminder of gnomish resourcefulness far from Ironforge."},kw={"azshara","blimo gadgetspring","durotar","jagged reef","jubie gadgetspring","makrura","murloc","ruined reaches"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:jagged-reef","zone:durotar","topic:murloc"},src={"Ruined Reaches"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-eldarath"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Eldarath",z="azshara",s="The Ruins of Eldarath are the shattered remains of a pre-Sundering Highborne city perched along the rocky bluffs of Azshara. Once a bastion of Kaldorei arcane scholarship, its fallen plazas and crumbling temples are now overrun by hostile naga. Scholars and adventurers brave the dangerous coastal ruins searching for inscribed tablets and forgotten relics of the ancient past.",h="The Ruins of Eldarath are the shattered remains of a pre-Sundering Highborne city perched along the rocky...",sec={{t="A Shattered Highborne Bastion",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, Eldarath was a flourishing night elven city. Renowned Highborne mages gathered here, carving their deepest arcane insights and fundamental magical rules into grand stone tablets left in public squares for their peers to study. During the apocalyptic War of the Ancients, the city became a battlefield between the Kaldorei Resistance and the demonic Burning Legion before the Sundering dropped much of Eldarath into the Bay of Storms. The portions that survived along the eastern cliffs have sat shunned by modern night elves for millennia, slowly claimed by creeping salt spray and ivy.",sp=0},{t="Naga Rule and Forgotten Relics",b="In recent times, vicious naga have emerged from the sea to seize the shattered streets of Eldarath, commanded by warlords lurking within nearby sanctuaries like the Temple of Zin-Malor. Despite the danger posed by the serpents, the ruins remain an irresistible lure for outsiders. The Explorers' League has dispatched Alliance adventurers into the broken courtyards to take rubbings of Eldarath's ancient arcane tablets. Whispers of lost treasures and lingering magical energy also drew the blue dragon Azuregos to the surrounding wilderness, further confirming that secrets of immense power still sleep beneath the ruins' cracked flagstones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Eldarath before it fell into ruins?",a="Before the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, Eldarath was a grand night elven city populated by the Highborne. It served as a center for arcane study and a fortified haven until the War of the Ancients and the sundering of the world devastated it.",al={"what was eldarath","eldarath history","eldarath origin"}},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Eldarath today?",a="Hostile naga have completely overrun the ruins, using the crumbling plazas and nearby structures like the Temple of Zin-Malor as coastal strongholds under the command of figures like Warlord Krellian.",al={"who lives in eldarath","what is in eldarath","eldarath mobs"}},{q="Why do scholars and explorers travel to Eldarath?",a="Scholars seek the preserved stone tablets left behind by ancient Highborne mages. These public markers contain fundamental rules of arcane magic and long-lost research, valuable enough that groups like the Dwarven Explorers' League send scouts to secure rubbings of the text.",al={"why go to eldarath","eldarath quests","what is at eldarath"}},{q="Why is the blue dragon Azuregos roaming near the ruins?",a="Azuregos is drawn to the extreme concentration of ancient arcane power lingering along Azshara's coast. Rumors suggest powerful relics from before the Sundering—possibly even vials touched by the ancient Well of Eternity—remain hidden within or around the ruins.",al={"why is azuregos here","azuregos eldarath","blue dragon in azshara"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Eldarath is a sacred, if cautionary, place of study: the stone tablets scattered across its plazas detail foundational arcane theories carved by the most gifted Highborne sorcerers before their empire fell.",["race:NightElf"]="These sun-bleached ruins serve as a bitter reminder of the hubris of the Highborne and the Sundering, long avoided by modern Kaldorei and now desecrated by the twisted naga."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","eldarath","explorers' league","highborne","kaldorei","naga","sundering","tablets"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-zin-malor","subzone:bay-of-storms","npc:azuregos","topic:highborne","topic:naga","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Eldarath"}}
E["subzone:shadowsong-shrine"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowsong Shrine",z="azshara",s="Shadowsong Shrine is a ruined hillside sanctuary situated in western Azshara, not far from the Ashenvale border. Haunted by the restless spirits of ancient Highborne, the site bears the illustrious name of the Shadowsong bloodline, though its true historical connection to them remains shrouded in mystery.",h="Shadowsong Shrine is a ruined hillside sanctuary situated in western Azshara, not far from the Ashenvale...",sec={{t="A Haunted Legacy",b="Perched upon a high hill overlooking the shattered lands of Azshara, the Shadowsong Shrine lies in ancient, overgrown ruin. Like much of the surrounding coast, it is plagued by the lingering apparitions of Highborne ghosts who wander among the fallen stonework, seeking to extinguish any mortal life that trespasses upon their domain. The shrine shares its name with two legendary figures of kaldorei history: Jarod Shadowsong, the reluctant general who led the night elf resistance during the War of the Ancients, and his sister Maiev, the unrelenting warden of Illidan Stormrage. Whether this sanctuary was erected in honor of their deeds or dates back to the family's standing before the Sundering is a secret lost to the ages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowsong Shrine?",a="It is an ancient night elf ruin located on an elevated rise in western Azshara. Today it stands crumbled and neglected, overrun by hostile Highborne specters.",al={"what is this place","shadowsong shrine info","ruins on the hill azshara"}},{q="Who is the shrine named after?",a="It shares its namesake with the storied Shadowsong lineage—most notably Jarod Shadowsong, hero of the War of the Ancients, and his elder sister Maiev, the famed warden. However, whether the shrine directly commemorates either of them is not definitively recorded.",al={"jarod shadowsong","maiev shadowsong","why shadowsong"}},{q="Why is the shrine haunted?",a="Like many ruins throughout Azshara, the site was devastated during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago. The spirits of the Highborne slain in the cataclysm remain bound to the stones, trapped in madness and hostility toward the living.",al={"why are there ghosts here","highborne ghosts azshara","ghosts at shadowsong shrine"}},{q="Where is the shrine located?",a="It sits atop a hill in western Azshara, east of the forested border with Ashenvale and not far from the outpost of Talrendis Point.",al={"where is shadowsong shrine","shadowsong shrine location","how to find shadowsong shrine"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the name Shadowsong commands profound respect due to Jarod's leadership during the War of the Ancients, making the desecration of this site by tormented Highborne ghosts especially tragic."},kw={"azshara","ghosts","highborne","jarod shadowsong","maiev","ruins","shadowsong","shrine"},rel={"zone:azshara","topic:highborne","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:alliance"},src={"Shadowsong Shrine"}}
E["subzone:shattered-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Shattered Strand",z="azshara",s="The Shattered Strand is a wild, rugged coastline flanking the northern rim of the Bay of Storms in Azshara. Dominated by crashing surf and crumbling ancient ruins, the beach crawls with hazardous marine beasts and tribal aquatic creatures.",h="The Shattered Strand is a wild, rugged coastline flanking the northern rim of the Bay of Storms in Azshara.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="Stretching along the northern edge of the Bay of Storms, the Shattered Strand is far from a peaceful shoreline. The rocky beaches and tidal shallows are heavily inhabited by aggressive wildlife, including towering sea giants, multi-headed hydras, and snapping makrura, alongside encampments of coastal murlocs. Crumbling elven architecture overlooks the waves, anchored by landmarks such as the ancient Temple of Arkkoran and the solitary Tower of Eldara. For travelers navigating Azshara's treacherous cliffs, descending to this isolated strip of coast means confronting some of the region's deadliest amphibious threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Shattered Strand located?",a="The Shattered Strand forms the northern coast of the Bay of Storms, situated in the eastern reaches of Azshara beneath the zone's towering clifftops.",al={"shattered strand location","where is shattered strand","shattered strand map"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Shattered Strand?",a="The shoreline is heavily prowled by vicious hydras, massive sea giants, armored makrura, and clusters of hostile murlocs patrolling the tidal flats.",al={"shattered strand mobs","what lives on shattered strand","shattered strand beasts"}},{q="What notable ruins can be found along the beach?",a="The coast is home to ancient highborne architecture, most prominently the Temple of Arkkoran and the nearby Tower of Eldara overlooking the bay.",al={"shattered strand ruins","buildings on shattered strand","landmarks shattered strand"}},{q="Is the Shattered Strand safe for casual exploration?",a="No. The beach is isolated, difficult to escape quickly due to the surrounding sheer cliffs, and tightly packed with predatory aquatic beasts and powerful giants.",al={"is shattered strand dangerous","shattered strand level"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The strand offers an untamed proving ground filled with formidable hydras and coastal beasts, ideal for those seeking powerful beasts or studying the predatory fauna of the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","hydras","makrura","murlocs","sea giants","shattered strand","temple of arkkoran","tower of eldara"},rel={"subzone:bay-of-storms","zone:azshara","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:tower-of-eldara","topic:murloc"},src={"Shattered Strand"}}
E["subzone:southfury-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Southfury River",z="azshara",s="The Southfury River is one of the most prominent waterways on central Kalimdor, carving a swift and wide path southward from the heights of Mount Hyjal. It forms the natural border separating Azshara from Ashenvale, as well as Durotar from the Barrens, before plunging into the Great Sea near Ratchet.",h="The Southfury River is one of the most prominent waterways on central Kalimdor, carving a swift and wide path...",sec={{t="A Vital Natural Divide",b="Beginning high in Mount Hyjal, the Southfury drops over dramatic cascades before coursing through central Kalimdor. Its roaring waters serve as a clear geographic divide, separating the sacred forests of Ashenvale from ancient Azshara, and dividing the arid hills of Durotar from the savanna of the Barrens. Only a few strategic bridges dare cross its swift currents—most notably the heavy span guarding the rear gates of Orgrimmar and the crossing connecting Durotar to the Barrens. The river eventually empties into the Great Sea via a cascading waterfall just northeast of the neutral port of Ratchet.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Importance",b="For the Horde, the Southfury is both a shield and a vital natural highway. It protects the western approaches of Durotar and Orgrimmar from immediate ground assault while supplying fresh mountain runoff through an otherwise scorched, sun-baked landscape. Just north of the western crossing into Orgrimmar lies a singular geographic crossroads where four major territories converge: Ashenvale, Azshara, Durotar, and the Barrens. Control over this churning waterway ensures supply lines between Orgrimmar and the outlying Horde settlements remain intact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Southfury River start and end?",a="The Southfury begins in the alpine reaches of Mount Hyjal, tumbling down dramatic waterfalls into the lowlands. It flows south between Ashenvale, Azshara, Durotar, and the Barrens before plunging into the Great Sea in a waterfall northeast of Ratchet.",al={"source of southfury river","where does southfury go","southfury mouth"}},{q="Which zones does the river border?",a="The river divides Ashenvale from Azshara in the north, and the Barrens from Durotar in the south. Notably, there is a point north of Orgrimmar's western bridge where all four territories meet along the riverbanks.",al={"what zones are on southfury","southfury border"}},{q="Where can travelers cross the Southfury River?",a="There are three primary bridges crossing the Southfury: one connecting Azshara into Ashenvale, one leading into the rear gates of Orgrimmar, and a major bridge connecting Durotar with the Barrens.",al={"southfury bridges","how to cross southfury","bridges over southfury"}},{q="Why is the river important to Orgrimmar?",a="The river provides a formidable natural barrier defending the western flank of Orgrimmar and Durotar. In addition, its fresh mountain waters are an invaluable lifeline across an otherwise dry and arid region.",al={"southfury orgrimmar","why horde cares about southfury"}},{q="What is the Southfury River?",a="The Southfury River is the most prominent waterway in central Kalimdor. Flowing south from the heights of Mount Hyjal, its swift, wide waters carve natural borders between the forests of Ashenvale and the ruins of Azshara before cutting down to divide Durotar from the Barrens. It ultimately empties into the Great Sea through a cascading waterfall just northeast of the goblin port of Ratchet.",al={"what is southfury river","southfury river overview","southfury river lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Southfury River dangerous?",a="The river itself is a swiftly flowing torrent with perilous, plunging waterfalls where it tumbles from Mount Hyjal and empties into the sea. Beyond the treacherous current, the lands on either side are rife with conflict and prowling beasts, making any unguided crossing far riskier than sticking to the fortified bridges.",al={"is southfury river dangerous","southfury river threats","southfury dangers"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Southfury River acts as Durotar's western defensive perimeter and the natural line of transit connecting the capital to the heart of the Barrens."},kw={"ashenvale","azshara","barrens","durotar","hyjal","orgrimmar","ratchet","southfury","southfury river"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:ashenvale","zone:azshara","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:ratchet","topic:horde"},src={"Southfury River"}}
E["subzone:southridge-beach"] = {t="subzone",n="Southridge Beach",z="azshara",s="Southridge Beach stretches along the southern shores of the Bay of Storms in central Azshara. Once a grand district of the ancient kaldorei city of Eldarath, its shattered ruins are now overrun by hostile naga, murlocs, and towering sea giants.",h="Southridge Beach stretches along the southern shores of the Bay of Storms in central Azshara.",sec={{t="A Drowned Shoreline",b="Southridge Beach forms the southern boundary of the turbulent Bay of Storms. Thousands of years ago, this coast was part of the magnificent Highborne city of Eldarath, but the Great Sundering broke the land and plunged most of its palaces beneath the tides. Today, crumbling marble pillars and weathered stone pavilions dot the sand. Rather than scholars and noble courtiers, the strand is contested by aggressive Spinescale naga, prowling makrura, vicious hydras, and scavenging murloc tribes. Even massive sea giants occasionally wander ashore from the deeps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Southridge Beach located?",a="Southridge Beach is situated in central Azshara, lining the southern edge of the Bay of Storms just beneath the mainland cliffs.",al={"southridge beach location","where is southridge beach","azshara southridge beach"}},{q="What ruins are scattered along the beach?",a="The stone columns and arches along the sand are the outer remnants of Eldarath, a once-great Highborne night elf city that was shattered and flooded during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago.",al={"southridge beach ruins","eldarath ruins beach","what are the ruins here"}},{q="What creatures live on Southridge Beach?",a="The shoreline is heavily occupied by the naga, alongside primitive murlocs, armored makrura, dangerous hydras, and the occasional roaming sea giant.",al={"mobs on southridge beach","enemies southridge beach","what lives here"}},{q="Why are there so many naga here?",a="The naga have surged from the ocean depths to reclaim the ruins of their former civilization across Azshara, establishing a firm military presence along the beaches of the Bay of Storms.",al={"why naga on beach","naga southridge beach","azshara naga"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruined architecture on Southridge Beach serves as a painful reminder of the heights and tragic fall of ancient Highborne civilization before the Great Sundering."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","eldarath","makrura","murloc","naga","sea giant","southridge beach"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:bay-of-storms","topic:naga","topic:murloc"},src={"Southridge Beach"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-arkkoran"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Arkkoran",z="azshara",s="The Temple of Arkkoran is an ancient night elven ruin resting on the northeastern cliffs of Azshara above the Shattered Strand. Originally built in honor of Elune, the crumbling structure has since been claimed by the towering sea giant Arkkoroc and his aquatic thralls.",h="The Temple of Arkkoran is an ancient night elven ruin resting on the northeastern cliffs of Azshara above the...",sec={{t="A Consecrated Ruin Claimed by the Sea",b="Like many of the grand ruins dotting Azshara's coast, the Temple of Arkkoran was once a sanctum dedicated to the moon goddess Elune before the Sundering shattered the ancient night elf empire. Today, its weathered marble steps and broken colonnades are overrun by tidal monstrosities. The sea giant Arkkoroc presides over the temple's highest level, surrounded by loyal makrura and vicious murlocs who violently defend the surrounding coastline from any land-dwelling intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Temple of Arkkoran originally built for?",a="Long before it became known by its current name, the structure was a night elven temple dedicated to the worship of Elune. It fell into ruins during the Great Sundering alongside the rest of the surrounding coastal civilization.",al={"temple of arkkoran history","who built temple of arkkoran","what is this temple"}},{q="Who is Arkkoroc?",a="Arkkoroc is a powerful sea giant who has made this former night elven temple his home. He resides on the highest platform of the ruins, commanding the surrounding shore and the coastal beasts that inhabit it.",al={"who is arkkoroc","arkkoroc sea giant","who rules arkkoran"}},{q="What creatures guard the temple grounds?",a="The temple and its surrounding terraces are patrolled by aggressive makrura and murlocs, including Arkkoran clackers, pincers, and muckdwellers. The surrounding beaches of the Shattered Strand are also home to hydras and other sea giants.",al={"temple of arkkoran mobs","what lives at temple of arkkoran","enemies at temple of arkkoran"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing a sacred house of Elune degraded into a nesting ground for makrura and sea giants is a bitter reminder of the splendor lost ten thousand years ago.",["class:Priest"]="Though ancient symbols of Elune linger among the weathered stones, no divine communion remains within these sea-battered ruins."},kw={"arkkoroc","azshara","elune","makrura","murloc","sea giant","shattered strand","temple of arkkoran"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:shattered-strand","topic:elune","topic:murloc"},src={"Temple of Arkkoran"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-zin-malor"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Zin-Malor",z="azshara",s="The Temple of Zin-Malor is an ancient night elven sanctuary located within the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara. Originally dedicated to the moon goddess Elune, the crumbling structure is now held by the Spitelash naga under the direct command of Warlord Krellian.",h="The Temple of Zin-Malor is an ancient night elven sanctuary located within the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Moon",b="Before the Great Sundering, the Temple of Zin-Malor stood as a grand house of worship dedicated to Elune. Its architecture closely mirrors both the nearby Temple of Arkkoran and the modern Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, bearing the graceful, sweeping stonework characteristic of pre-Sundering night elven civilization. Today, however, its moonlit marble is weathered and broken, overtaken by the serpent-bodied Spitelash naga. These invaders have claimed the holy grounds for themselves, turning a place of quiet reflection into a militarized redoubt.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Crystal and Ancient Vaults",b="The temple once housed the renowned Crystal of Zin-Malor, a potent artifact that was carried away long ago to Kel'Theril in Winterspring. Beneath the temple's sunlit flagstones lies a royal vault containing forgotten relics of the Highborne. Among these antiquities sits an ornate, empty chest of pandaren craftsmanship—the final diplomatic gift sent by the pandaren before severing relations with the Highborne, offering the silent counsel that the elves did not truly require arcane power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Temple of Zin-Malor today?",a="The temple is occupied by the Spitelash naga tribe. Their leader in the region, Warlord Krellian, resides within the temple structure itself.",al={"who is at zin-malor","who lives in zin malor","who is the boss in zin malor"}},{q="What was the temple used for originally?",a="It was originally built before the Great Sundering by the ancient night elves as a sacred place of worship honoring Elune, the moon goddess.",al={"who built zin-malor","what was zin-malor"}},{q="Why does it look so much like the temple in Darnassus?",a="The Temple of Zin-Malor shares classic night elven architectural roots with the Temple of Arkkoran. The modern Temple of the Moon in Darnassus was deliberately built following this same traditional, sacred layout.",al={"darnassus temple resemblance","architecture of zin-malor"}},{q="What is the Crystal of Zin-Malor?",a="It is an ancient magical relic that originally resided within the temple. Long ago, it was stolen away by the residents of Kel'Theril, deep in the frozen lands of Winterspring.",al={"where is the crystal of zin malor","zin malor crystal"}},{q="What is hidden beneath the temple?",a="Beneath the temple lies an underground royal vault holding ancient Highborne relics, including a historic gift left behind by the pandaren before they cut ties with the night elves.",al={"vault of zin malor","underground zin malor"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Walking the ruins of Zin-Malor offers a bitter reminder of the Highborne era and the tragic corruption of the naga, who now desecrate what was once holy ground dedicated to Elune.",["class:Priest"]="Priesthood traditions honoring Elune run deep in these stones, bearing the exact sanctuary layouts that modern sisterhoods still preserve in Darnassus."},kw={"arkkoran","azshara","crystal of zin-malor","eldarath","krellian","pandaren chest","spitelash","zin-malor"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:elune","topic:naga","topic:highborne","zone:azshara","zone:winterspring"},src={"Temple of Zin-Malor"}}
E["subzone:thalassian-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Thalassian Base Camp",z="azshara",s="Tucked onto a high ridge in northern Azshara, the Thalassian Base Camp serves as the staging ground for an expedition of blood elves unearthing ancient arcane relics. Though initially funded under an agreement with the Horde, the camp's leadership quickly broke faith once digging commenced. Now, amidst their red pavilions and pulverized magical artifacts, darker summoning practices hint at their true objectives.",h="Tucked onto a high ridge in northern Azshara, the Thalassian Base Camp serves as the staging ground for an...",sec={{t="A Fractured Accord",b="The blood elf expedition nestled east of Ursolan was not supposed to be hostile to travelers from Orgrimmar. Their leader, Magus Rimtori, negotiated a formal pact with the Horde: in exchange for supply lines, funding, and armed escort through Azshara's treacherous wildlands, her researchers would share whatever magical riches they uncovered. Instead, as soon as the base camp was fortified and the first relics were pried from the elven ruins, Rimtori reneged entirely, driving away Horde emissaries. While Rimtori searches deeper reaches with an armed retinue, Magister Hawkhelm keeps watch over the ridge, guarding the encampment against retribution.",sp=0},{t="Dust and Demonology",b="The blood elves did not come merely to catalog history. They possess an unusual technique for pulverizing recovered magical curios into Glittering Dust—a refined powder distinctly different from common enchanting residue, which has already caught the curiosity of Archmage Xylem. More alarmingly, higher up the camp's ridges sits a Kaldorei Tome of Summoning. Far from an academic study of Highborne relics, the tome reveals a sinister willingness to pierce the veil and summon demonic entities directly into the ruins of Azshara.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are blood elves here in Azshara?",a="They are part of an arcane excavation led by Magus Rimtori. They traveled across Kalimdor to exploit the ruins of ancient Kalimdor for potent magical artifacts, seeking power to harvest and siphon in the wake of the Sunwell's destruction.",al={"why are there blood elves in azshara","thalassian base camp purpose","who lives here"}},{q="Why is the Horde hostile to this camp?",a="Magus Rimtori took Horde coin and resources under the promise of sharing the expedition's discoveries. Once her forces were safely established in northern Azshara, she broke the agreement, refused any tribute, and left the Horde looking for revenge.",al={"why do horde attack thalassian base camp","magus rimtori betrayal","betrayed quest lore"}},{q="Who leads the Thalassian Base Camp?",a="The overarching leader of the expedition is Magus Rimtori, though she frequently ventures across Azshara flanked by personal bodyguards. In her absence, day-to-day command of the camp falls to Magister Hawkhelm.",al={"who is in charge","camp boss","magister hawkhelm"}},{q="What is Glittering Dust?",a="It is an arcane residue produced through the blood elves' specialized method of crushing enchanted relics. Unlike the standard dust gathered through traditional enchanting disenchantment, its unique properties have drawn the keen interest of the eccentric Archmage Xylem.",al={"magic dust xylem","glittering dust lore","why crush magical items"}},{q="What is the Kaldorei Tome of Summoning on the ridge?",a="Perched on a ridge overlooking the camp, this ancient tome can be used to call forth demons into the area. Its presence exposes that Rimtori's expedition is dabbling in far darker pursuits than simple historical recovery.",al={"book on the hill","kaldorei tome","demon book azshara"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde does not take broken oaths lightly; Magus Rimtori took your coin and gave back only treachery, making this camp an active target for retribution.",["class:Mage"]="The blood elves' unique refinement of artifacts into Glittering Dust offers a rare, if dangerous, glimpse into Thalassian techniques that interest even Archmage Xylem."},kw={"azshara","betrayed","glittering dust","hawkhelm","magister hawkhelm","magus rimtori","rimtori","thalassian base camp","ursolan"},rel={"npc:magus-rimtori","zone:azshara","npc:archmage-xylem","subzone:ursolan","topic:horde"},src={"Thalassian Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-eldara"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Eldara",z="azshara",s="The Tower of Eldara is an ancient, sealed night elven spire situated on the far northeastern promontory overlooking the Bay of Storms in Azshara. Though long abandoned, its sturdy stone architecture has survived the Sundering, standing silent above coasts roamed by aggressive coastal beasts.",h="The Tower of Eldara is an ancient, sealed night elven spire situated on the far northeastern promontory...",sec={{t="A Relic of Ancient Azshara",b="Perched on a remote cliff edge northeast of the Bay of Storms, the Tower of Eldara stands as a lonely testament to the vast kaldorei empire that once dominated this coastline. Like much of Azshara's ruined architecture, it fell into disuse following the Great Sundering thousands of years ago. Today, the entrance remains firmly closed and barred against the outside world, giving no hint of whatever relics or chambers lie sealed inside. The surrounding shores are fraught with danger, prowled constantly by wandering murlocs, clawing makrura, and predatory hydras that keep all but the most daring travelers away.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Eldara?",a="It is an ancient night elven tower located on the northeastern cliff edge of Azshara, overlooking the Bay of Storms. It was built prior to the Great Sundering as part of the sprawling kaldorei empire that once spanned the region.",al={"tower of eldara lore","what is this tower","eldara tower"}},{q="Can you enter the Tower of Eldara?",a="No. The tower stands closed and firmly sealed against outsiders. Whatever chambers or vaults remain intact within are barred from modern explorers.",al={"can i go inside tower of eldara","how to open tower of eldara","is the tower open"}},{q="What threats wander around the tower?",a="The rocky bluffs and nearby sandy beaches surrounding the promontory are heavily patrolled by hostile murlocs, armored makrura, and coastal hydras.",al={"mobs near tower of eldara","enemies around eldara","bay of storms creatures"}},{q="Where exactly is the tower located?",a="You can find it on the far eastern tip of land jutting into the Great Sea, just northeast across the waters of the Bay of Storms in Azshara.",al={"tower of eldara location","where is tower of eldara","how to find eldara"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Tower of Eldara is a poignant reminder of the grand empire your ancestors ruled before Queen Azshara and the Highborne shattered the ancient world.",["class:Mage"]="Like many Highborne structures across Azshara, the sealed tower likely once hummed with arcane studies before being locked away from mortal meddling."},kw={"azshara","bay of storms","eldara","highborne","kaldorei","ruins","tower of eldara"},rel={"zone:azshara","subzone:bay-of-storms","topic:murloc"},src={"Tower of Eldara"}}
E["subzone:ursolan"] = {t="subzone",n="Ursolan",z="azshara",s="Ursolan is a sprawling Timbermaw furbolg settlement situated in western Azshara, just east of Timbermaw Hold. Bisected by a deep ravine, the encampment honors the bear Ancient Ursol and serves as a vital stronghold for uncorrupted furbolgs defending their territory from outside incursions.",h="Ursolan is a sprawling Timbermaw furbolg settlement situated in western Azshara, just east of Timbermaw Hold.",sec={{t="Bastion of the Bear",b="Perched on the rugged bluffs of western Azshara, Ursolan constitutes the eastern branch of the Timbermaw tribe's domain, connecting directly through Timbermaw Hold to Bear's Head in the south. Named after the revered bear Ancient Ursol, this camp represents a rare haven of sanity among Kalimdor's furbolg populations, which have largely fallen victim to demonic corruption. The village spans both rims of a dramatic earthen chasm, where the Timbermaw vigilantly guard their borders against encroaching interlopers, including intrusive researchers from the night elven camp of Talrendis.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Ursolan?",a="Ursolan is inhabited by the Timbermaw furbolgs, one of the last remaining tribes of furbolgs that has managed to resist the demonic corruption plaguing Kalimdor.",al={"who is at ursolan","ursolan inhabitants","ursolan furbolgs"}},{q="Why is this area called Ursolan?",a="The settlement is named in honor of Ursol, one of the twin bear demigods deeply venerated by the furbolg race.",al={"ursolan name origin","who is ursolan named after","meaning of ursolan"}},{q="What is the deep gorge running through the camp?",a="Ursolan is split by a deep scar in the earth. Down within this ravine, Talrendis biologists from the nearby night elven encampment can often be found conducting field studies.",al={"canyon in ursolan","ravine in ursolan","chasm ursolan"}},{q="How does Ursolan connect to the rest of the Timbermaw territory?",a="Ursolan sits directly east of the Azshara entrance to Timbermaw Hold, linking their northern presence through the mountain tunnels down to Bear's Head in the south.",al={"ursolan connection","how to get to timbermaw hold from ursolan"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids hold profound respect for the patrons of Ursolan, as the twin bear Ancients Ursol and Ursoc are central figures in nature worship and bear form mastery.",["race:NightElf"]="Although night elves revere the bear Ancients, tensions exist on the ground, evidenced by the Talrendis researchers examining the ravine under the wary eyes of the furbolgs."},kw={"azshara","furbolg","ravine","talrendis","timbermaw","ursol","ursolan"},rel={"subzone:timbermaw-hold","topic:furbolg","subzone:bear-s-head","zone:azshara"},src={"Ursolan"}}
E["subzone:valormok"] = {t="subzone",n="Valormok",z="azshara",s="Valormok is a remote Horde outpost established in the rugged northwest reaches of Azshara. Positioned north of the Haldarr Encampment, this windswept settlement serves as a staging ground for scouts and adventurers braving the cursed, ancient ruins of the coast.",h="Valormok is a remote Horde outpost established in the rugged northwest reaches of Azshara.",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="Perched among the autumn-colored trees of Azshara, Valormok represents the Horde's tentative interest in a hostile and largely forsaken territory. Life here is bleak and fraught with peril; the camp is lightly fortified and constantly exposed to nearby satyrs, nagas, and prowling beasts. Despite these hardships, its stationed warriors hold the ground, acting as a crucial flight hub and forward bastion connecting Orgrimmar with the wilder stretches of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Treachery and Retribution",b="The camp was recently struck by a devastating betrayal. Belgrom Rockmaul originally dispatched Horde warriors alongside a blood elf named Magus Rimtori to uncover ancient treasures and powerful relics among the ruins. Rimtori turned upon her escort, butchering the warriors to claim the artifacts for herself. Led by Ag'tor Bloodfist, the survivors in Valormok now plot vengeance against Rimtori and her cohort entrenched at the nearby Thalassian Base Camp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Valormok?",a="Valormok is an isolated Horde settlement located in northwestern Azshara. It provides a vital flight master connection and serves as an operations base for Horde travelers surveying the ancient coastal wilderness.",al={"valormok azshara","what is this camp","horde base in azshara"}},{q="Who leads the encampment?",a="The outpost is overseen by Ag'tor Bloodfist, an orc warrior tasked with maintaining the Horde's foothold and securing vengeance for his slain comrades.",al={"who is in charge","valormok leader","agtor bloodfist"}},{q="Why were so many Horde warriors killed here?",a="Belgrom Rockmaul had dispatched warriors to escort the blood elf Magus Rimtori in a search for relics. Rimtori betrayed and slaughtered her escort to hoard the power and wealth of Azshara for herself, leaving the garrison heavily diminished.",al={"what happened to the guards","valormok massacre","rimtori betrayal"}},{q="Where does the flight master connect to?",a="Valormok's wind rider master offers direct flight connections across Kalimdor, including routes to Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, Splintertree Post, Bloodvenom Post, and Everlook.",al={"valormok flight paths","where can i fly from valormok"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Valormok is the primary sanctuary for Horde adventurers navigating Azshara's treacherous ruins, offering flight masters and missions of vengeance.",["race:Orc"]="The outpost stands as a grim test of endurance for orcs stationed far from Orgrimmar, bound by honor to avenge their betrayed kin."},kw={"ag'tor bloodfist","azshara","belgrom rockmaul","flight master","jediga","magus rimtori","valormok"},rel={"zone:azshara","npc:magus-rimtori","subzone:thalassian-base-camp","subzone:haldarr-encampment","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:bloodvenom-post","topic:horde"},src={"Valormok"}}
E["topic:cenarius"] = {t="topic",n="Cenarius",z="azshara",s="Cenarius, the Lord of the Forest, is the ancient demigod son of Elune and Malorne who taught the night elves the secrets of druidism. For thousands of years he served as the great patron of mortal druids and guardian of the wilderness before falling in battle during the Third War.",h="Cenarius, the Lord of the Forest, is the ancient demigod son of Elune and Malorne who taught the night elves...",sec={{t="Son of Heaven and Earth",b="Cenarius was born to Elune, the goddess of the moon, and the great white stag demigod Malorne. Because Cenarius was bound to the mortal world, Elune placed him in the care of Malorne, while Ysera the Dreamer embraced him as a foster mother and guided him through the infinite paths of the Emerald Dream. Blessed with powers over living wood and earth, Cenarius fathered the Keepers of the Grove and the dryads, forever tying his bloodline to the wild places of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The First Druid",b="Though Cenarius briefly taught ancient night elves and the early tauren, mortal races repeatedly turned away from nature toward arcane monuments. Millennia later, three youths—Malfurion Stormrage, his twin Illidan, and Tyrande Whisperwind—sought out the demigod of legend. Cenarius recognized Malfurion's exceptional heart and trained him as the first mortal druid. When Queen Azshara and her Highborne unleashed the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, Cenarius marshaled Kalimdor's wild demigods to fight alongside mortal defenders.",sp=0},{t="The Fall at Ashenvale",b="For ten millennia following the Great Sundering, Cenarius watched over Kalimdor and nurtured the Cenarion Circle alongside Malfurion. That vigilant watch ended during the Third War when the Warsong clan began harvesting timber in Ashenvale. Outraged by the destruction of sacred woodlands, Cenarius drove the invaders back until Grom Hellscream and his warriors partook of Mannoroth's demonic blood. Infused with demonic fury, the corrupted orcs overwhelmed the demigod and struck him down, casting a dark pall across nature's defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cenarius?",a="Cenarius is an ancient demigod of nature, the patron saint of druids, and the guardian of Azeroth's wilderness. Born of the moon goddess Elune and the demigod Malorne, he was fostered by the Dragon Aspect Ysera and became the supreme champion of the wild lands.",al={"who is cenarius","cenarius lore","cenarius backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Who are Cenarius's children?",a="His sons are the Keepers of the Grove, such as Keeper Remulos and Ordanus, while his daughters are the fey dryads. The centaur race traces their lineage to his son Zaetar, making Cenarius their grandfather.",al={"cenarius children","keepers of the grove father","cenarius daughters"}},{q="How did Malfurion learn druidism from Cenarius?",a="Before the War of the Ancients, Malfurion sought out the mythical demigod alongside Illidan and Tyrande. Recognizing Malfurion's rare dedication and balance, Cenarius instructed him in the sacred arts of nature, making him the first mortal druid.",al={"malfurion first druid","how did malfurion learn druidism"}},{q="What happened to Cenarius in the Third War?",a="During the Third War, the orcish Warsong clan harvested timber in Ashenvale, provoking Cenarius's wrath. Desperate to overcome the demigod's power, chieftain Grom Hellscream drank from a pool tainted with the blood of Mannoroth, gaining demonic strength to slay Cenarius.",al={"how did cenarius die","who killed cenarius","cenarius death"}},{q="What is Cenarius's connection to the tauren?",a="Ancient bovine ancestors of the tauren lived on central Kalimdor alongside Cenarius. When they reunited with the demigod in subsequent generations, those who studied under him learned the earliest rudiments of natural druidic magic.",al={"tauren cenarius","did cenarius teach tauren"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle is the monastic order of druids dedicated to preserving nature's balance, studying the Emerald Dream, and guarding the sacred forests. It was founded in honor of Cenarius by his disciple Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"what is cenarion circle","who founded cenarion circle"},it="allies"},{q="Where did Cenarius come from?",a="Cenarius was born from the union of Elune, the moon goddess, and the white stag demigod Malorne. Because he belonged more to the mortal realm than the heavens, Elune yielded his upbringing to Malorne and Ysera the Dreamer. Ysera raised Cenarius within the Emerald Dream, tutoring him in its deep mysteries. Over millennia, the Lord of the Forest wandered Azeroth's wilds, teaching the natural ways to ancient peoples and standing beside mortal defenders through catastrophic conflicts like the War of the Ancients.",al={"cenarius origin","cenarius history","birth of cenarius"},it="history",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Every druid traces their path directly back to Cenarius, the eternal patron whose lessons to Malfurion established the druidic ways.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei revere Cenarius as a divine guide and ally whose death at the hands of the Warsong orcs remains an unforgiven tragedy.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren myth speaks fondly of Cenarius, remembering an ancient kinship and shared reverence for the Earth Mother before the dawn of modern history.",["race:Orc"]="The slaying of Cenarius by Grom Hellscream stands as a grim reminder of the blood curse and the destructive costs of demonic servitude."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarion","cenarius","druid","elune","malfurion","malorne","remulos","ysera"},rel={"npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:elune","npc:remulos","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:emerald-dream","quest:1088"},src={"Cenarius"}}
E["zone:azshara"] = {t="zone",n="Azshara",z="azshara",s="Azshara is a rugged, windswept coastline in northeastern Kalimdor cloaked in vibrant, perpetual autumn foliage. Once part of the glorious night elven capital before the Great Sundering shattered it into the sea, it remains a dangerous wilderness littered with ancient ruins, brooding naga, and isolated practitioners of magic. Both the Horde and the Alliance maintain precarious outposts along its borders, wary of the restless ghosts and ocean horrors lurking within.",h="Azshara is a rugged, windswept coastline in northeastern Kalimdor cloaked in vibrant, perpetual autumn...",sec={{t="A Drowned Empire",b="Ten thousand years ago, this coast was the beating heart of the kaldorei civilization, surrounding the royal capital of Zin-Azshari. When Queen Azshara and her Highborne court drew the Burning Legion into Azeroth, the resulting War of the Ancients culminated in the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity. The sea thundered inward, swallowing most of the magnificent city and leaving behind fractured cliffs, treacherous coral reefs, and waterlogged spires. The survivors renamed the ruined landscape after their fallen monarch, branding it as a cursed monument to pride and catastrophic betrayal.",sp=0},{t="Autumn Splendor and Hidden Perils",b="Azshara is famous for its stunning crimson, orange, and gold canopy, giving the impression of an eternal autumn unbroken by changing seasons. Beneath this tranquil canopy, however, lies an inhospitable expanse. Corrupted satyrs practice dark rituals in forested hollows, lingering Highborne apparitions haunt drowned foundations, and Spitelash naga prowl the shallow reefs of the Coral Sea. Ferocious beasts, giant hydras, and mountain giants roam unchecked across the highlands and ivory beaches.",sp=0},{t="A Realm of Exiles and Outcasts",b="Because of its isolation and harsh terrain, Azshara draws recluse figures pursuing forgotten crafts or watching over dangerous powers. The enigmatic Archmage Xylem inhabits a secluded tower perched high above the cliffs, testing promising spellcasters and cunning rogues alike. Farther along the coast, the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes watches the waves from a barren isle, while the immense sea giant Lord Arkkoroc demands blood sacrifices from his temple overlooking the churning waters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are all the trees red and orange here?",a="Azshara is cloaked in a perpetual autumn. The vibrant orange, gold, and red canopy never sheds its leaves, giving the coastal woods a strikingly beautiful yet melancholy atmosphere that has persisted for thousands of years.",al={"why is azshara autumn","why are trees red","azshara fall foliage"}},{q="How did Azshara become a ruin?",a="This coastline once formed the outskirts of the kaldorei capital, Zin-Azshari. During the War of the Ancients, the Well of Eternity imploded during the Great Sundering, sundering the continent and sending vast portions of the city tumbling into the sea.",al={"what happened to azshara","why is azshara broken","azshara history"}},{q="Who rules Azshara today?",a="No single faction holds dominion over the territory. The Alliance maintains a small watch at Talrendis Point near Ashenvale, while the Horde operates out of the encampment of Valormok. The surrounding land is dominated by dangerous Spitelash naga, violent satyrs, and untamed monsters.",al={"who controls azshara","who runs azshara","is azshara alliance or horde"}},{q="Who is Archmage Xylem?",a="Archmage Xylem is an eccentric human sorcerer residing in a remote cliffside tower overlooking Azshara. Unaligned with regional politics, he aids visiting mages and rogues in unlocking unique martial and arcane potential through challenging trials.",al={"xylem azshara","mage tower azshara","wizard in azshara"}},{q="What is the blue dragon doing in the ruins?",a="The great blue dragon Azuregos and his brood watch over the ancient ruins of Eldarath. He fiercely protects the powerful Highborne magical artifacts still buried in the rubble from being plundered by mortal hands.",al={"azuregos in azshara","blue dragon azshara","dragon in eldarath"}},{q="Why do the night elves consider this land cursed?",a="The kaldorei consider Azshara cursed because it bears the name and architectural legacy of their treacherous Queen Azshara, whose pact with the Burning Legion shattered their empire and brought ruin to the world.",al={"is azshara cursed","why do night elves hate azshara","night elf curse azshara"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every drowned pillar and wailing Highborne shade in Azshara serves as a grim, haunting testament to Queen Azshara's reckless arrogance and the cataclysmic ruin of the ancient kaldorei civilization.",["class:Mage"]="The shattered stones of Eldarath still crackle with forgotten Highborne sorcery, and high above the cliffs, the reclusive Archmage Xylem tests those seeking mastery of arcane teleportation and spellcraft.",["profession:Mining"]="The steep coastal cliffs and jagged ridges of Azshara are rich in precious mineral veins, containing abundant deposits of Mithril, Truesilver, and Thorium.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Azshara's perpetual autumn climate sustains rare and potent herbs, including Dreamfoil, Golden Sansam, Mountain Silversage, and Purple Lotus among the ruins."},kw={"azshara","azuregos","bay of storms","coral sea","eldarath","highborne","spitelash","talrendis point","valormok","xylem"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","subzone:ruins-of-eldarath","subzone:bay-of-storms","subzone:temple-of-arkkoran","subzone:lake-mennar","zone:winterspring"},src={"Azshara (Classic)","Azshara"}}
